RCx8 assembler

Usage: rcx8asm inputfile [outputfile] [-l listingfile]
  outputfile defaults to out.prg, a listing file of - writes to stdout.

Source format
  # comment                       comment up to the end of the line
  .comment "text"                 comment block stored in the binary
  .data 0x0100                    code/data segment loaded at the given address
  .include "other.asm"            include a file (relative to the including file)
  label:                          label, may be followed by a statement
  db 1, 0xAB, 0b101, "text"       bytes and strings (not zero terminated)
  dw 0x1234, label                16 bit words
  ds "text"                       zero terminated string
  fim R0 lo(table)                lo()/hi() give the low/high byte of a value
  jun loop+3                      one label plus/minus constants
  wmp 5  /  rdr P7                ports as number or Pn
  Mnemonics, registers and ports are case insensitive, labels are not.
  A label called "main" is required, it is the program start address.

Output format (little endian, see the RCX8 loader)
  0x7000 pc | 0x1000 len bytes (comment) | 0x2000 offset len bytes (data) | 0x0000

Tests: tests/run_tests.sh path/to/rcx8asm
